# The build context is sent to the Docker daemon in full and `COPY . .` pulls it
# into the build stage. None of the following belongs in either.

# Private planning and career-strategy notes. These never reach the runtime
# image (only the binary is copied out), but keeping them out of the build stage
# means they are not one Dockerfile edit away from shipping.
local/

# Secrets and local configuration. Production config comes from
# .env.production on the droplet, via compose's env_file.
.env
.env.*

# Version control history — large, and the build needs none of it.
.git
.gitignore

# Build output. `app` alone is ~14MB of compiled Go being uploaded for nothing.
app
tmp/

# Local databases; the real one lives on a named volume.
db.sqlite

# The résumé is bind-mounted from the droplet, not baked into the image.
*.pdf

# Docs and agent configuration are not inputs to the build.
docs/
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
README.md
.github/
.scratch/
